# Marshal — the GCP-backed deployments runtime. All config is env vars; there is no
# database (the only state is the S3-compatible bucket below).

# Server
MARSHAL_PORT=# port to listen on. Defaults to ${NEXT_PUBLIC_HEXCLAVE_PORT_PREFIX:-81}47. Standalone only — on Vercel the platform owns the listener (see README.md)
MARSHAL_API_KEY=# bearer credential the backend must present on every /v1 request. Required: Marshal refuses to start if unset
CRON_SECRET=# value Vercel's scheduler sends as its bearer token. Accepted ONLY on /v1/maintenance/*, so it need not equal MARSHAL_API_KEY. Unset means the platform sends no credential and the project-pool crons cannot run
MARSHAL_WEBHOOK_SECRET=# HMAC key for per-build webhook tokens. Defaults to MARSHAL_API_KEY (fine outside prod)
HEXCLAVE_MARSHAL_DATA_ENCRYPTION_KEY=# 64 hex chars (32 bytes), separate from S3 credentials; encrypts stored service environments and authenticates authoritative control-plane state. Required
MARSHAL_PUBLIC_URL=# stable base URL builder VMs use to call the completion webhook (e.g. https://marshal.example.com). Required for real GCP builds; unused by the mock builder
MARSHAL_ENV_ID=# environment discriminator baked into managed resource names ("dev", "stg", "prd"). Must differ per environment
MARSHAL_ALLOW_MOCKS=# set to 1 only in development/test environments to permit the mock builder or existing-project test override; mocks fail closed when unset

# Google Cloud (credentials resolve in this order: workload identity federation, then
# GOOGLE_APPLICATION_CREDENTIALS, then the GCE metadata server). Marshal creates one project
# per namespace.
HEXCLAVE_MARSHAL_GCP_WORKLOAD_IDENTITY_AUDIENCE=# full WIF provider resource, "//iam.googleapis.com/projects/<number>/locations/global/workloadIdentityPools/<pool>/providers/<provider>". Set with the service account below to authenticate a host that has no metadata server (Vercel); leave both empty otherwise
HEXCLAVE_MARSHAL_GCP_WORKLOAD_IDENTITY_SERVICE_ACCOUNT=# controller service account the federated identity impersonates, e.g. marshal-controller@<platform-project>.iam.gserviceaccount.com. Setting only one of these two is a hard error, not a fallback to the other credential modes
HEXCLAVE_MARSHAL_GCP_WORKLOAD_IDENTITY_TOKEN_ENV=# env var to read the host's OIDC assertion from when a request carries no x-vercel-oidc-token header (builds, local development). Defaults to VERCEL_OIDC_TOKEN
HEXCLAVE_MARSHAL_GCP_BILLING_ACCOUNT=# billing account id or billingAccounts/<id> attached to each tenant project. Required outside existing-project tests
HEXCLAVE_MARSHAL_GCP_PROJECT_PARENT=# recommended folders/<id> parent for tenant projects; organizations/<id> is also accepted. Empty creates parentless projects when IAM permits
HEXCLAVE_MARSHAL_GCP_PROJECT_PREFIX=# globally unique project-id prefix. Defaults to hxc-tenant
HEXCLAVE_MARSHAL_GCP_PROJECT_POOL_SIZE=# fully provisioned tenant projects kept ready for instant assignment (Google's multi-tenant recommendation). 0-100; defaults to 0 (first deploy into a namespace provisions its project synchronously). Production sets 5-10. The pool is filled by the /v1/maintenance/project-pool crons, so a non-zero size does nothing unless they are scheduled (see README.md)
HEXCLAVE_MARSHAL_GCP_PLATFORM_PROJECT_ID=# existing platform project that owns the shared global IP, URL map, HTTPS proxy, and Certificate Manager resources. Required
HEXCLAVE_MARSHAL_GCP_REGION=# Cloud Run, Artifact Registry, NEG, and subnet region. Defaults to us-central1
HEXCLAVE_MARSHAL_GCP_ZONE=# Compute Engine zone within HEXCLAVE_MARSHAL_GCP_REGION. Defaults to <region>-a
HEXCLAVE_MARSHAL_GCP_NETWORK=# per-tenant VPC name. Defaults to hexclave-runtime
HEXCLAVE_MARSHAL_GCP_SUBNETWORK=# per-tenant subnetwork name. Defaults to hexclave-runtime
HEXCLAVE_MARSHAL_GCP_EXISTING_PROJECT_ID_FOR_TESTS=# skips project provisioning for a disposable pre-created project. Requires MARSHAL_ALLOW_MOCKS=1; never use in production
HEXCLAVE_MARSHAL_GCP_MOCK_URL=# local GCP REST simulator URL, or "local" to derive localhost:<port-prefix>48. Requires MARSHAL_ALLOW_MOCKS=1; never use in production
HEXCLAVE_MARSHAL_GCP_MOCK_TOKEN=# token shared with the local GCP simulator. Defaults to the public development token when the mock URL is set
MARSHAL_BUILDER=# "gcp" (ephemeral BuildKit VM, the default) or "mock" (instant fake digest — for dev/e2e; non-prod only)

# Bucket (S3-compatible; Cloudflare R2 in production, the s3mock container locally)
MARSHAL_S3_ENDPOINT=# S3 API endpoint URL. Required
MARSHAL_S3_REGION=# S3 region ("auto" for R2). Defaults to auto
MARSHAL_S3_ACCESS_KEY_ID=# Required
MARSHAL_S3_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY=# Required
MARSHAL_S3_BUCKET=# bucket holding specs/, uploads/, builds/, domains/. Required
MARSHAL_S3_FORCE_PATH_STYLE=# set to 1 for path-style addressing (required for the s3mock container)
